-- coa5-ch4-supplementary.l4: Companies Act 2006, Part 10, Chapter 4, "Supplementary": ss 223 to 226 (lines 2928-2948 of ukpga-2006-46.txt):
-- shadow directors (s 223), accidental failure to send a memorandum (s 224), approval required under more than one provision (s 225),
-- and s 226 (the text shows dots only).
--
-- SOURCE: a plain-text rendering of the Act from legislation.gov.uk made by a converter script; not the official text.
-- HOW TO READ AN ANSWER: see coa5-loans-exceptions.l4 (JUST TRUE, JUST FALSE and NOTHING as the rule of 2026-10-29 reads them).

§ `Chapter 4 supplementary (ss 223 to 226)`

-- ======================================================================================================================
-- s 223 Transactions requiring members' approval: application of provisions to shadow directors
-- ======================================================================================================================

DECLARE `s 223(1) provisions` IS ONE OF
    `s 223(1)(a) sections 188 and 189 (directors' service contracts)`
    `s 223(1)(b) sections 190 to 196 (property transactions)`
    `s 223(1)(c) sections 197 to 214 (loans etc)`
    `s 223(1)(d) sections 215 to 222 (payments for loss of office)`
    `s 223(1) some other provision`

-- The shadow director answer is s 251's (this part): an input here.
-- src:2930 | (1) For the purposes of—
-- src:2931 | (a) sections 188 and 189 (directors' service contracts),
-- src:2932 | (b) sections 190 to 196 (property transactions),
-- src:2933 | (c) sections 197 to 214 (loans etc), and
-- src:2934 | (d) sections 215 to 222 (payments for loss of office),
-- src:2935 | a shadow director is treated as a director.
@ref s 223(1) a shadow director is treated as a director (src:2930-2935)
GIVEN provision IS A `s 223(1) provisions`
      `s 251 the person is a shadow director` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 223(1) the shadow director is treated as a director for the provision` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF provision EQUALS `s 223(1) some other provision`
        THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "For the purposes of— (a) sections 188 and 189 ..., (b) sections 190 to 196 ..., (c) sections 197 to 214 ..., and (d) sections 215 to 222"
        IF `s 251 the person is a shadow director` EQUALS JUST TRUE
        THEN JUST TRUE
        IF `s 251 the person is a shadow director` EQUALS NOTHING
        THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the person is a shadow director is s 251's answer
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "a shadow director is treated as a director" (the subsection speaks only of a shadow director)

DECLARE `s 223(2) what was lost` IS ONE OF
    `s 223(2) loss of office as a director`
    `s 223(2) loss of a person's status as a shadow director`

-- src:2936 | (2) Any reference in those provisions to loss of office as a director does not apply in relation to loss of a person's status as a shadow director.
@ref s 223(2) loss of status as a shadow director (src:2936-2936)
GIVEN lost IS A `s 223(2) what was lost`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 223(2) a reference to loss of office as a director applies to the loss` MEANS
    CONSIDER lost
    WHEN `s 223(2) loss of a person's status as a shadow director` THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Any reference in those provisions to loss of office as a director does not apply in relation to loss of a person's status as a shadow director"
    WHEN `s 223(2) loss of office as a director` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the subsection says only that the reference does not apply to loss of status as a shadow director

-- ======================================================================================================================
-- s 224 Approval by written resolution: accidental failure to send memorandum
-- ======================================================================================================================

-- src:2942 | (2) Subsection (1) has effect subject to any provision of the company's articles.
@ref s 224(2) subject to the articles (src:2942-2942)
GIVEN `a provision of the company's articles deals with the matter` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 224(2) subsection (1) has effect subject to a provision of the articles` MEANS
    IF `a provision of the company's articles deals with the matter`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Subsection (1) has effect subject to any provision of the company's articles"

-- src:2938 | (1) Where—
-- src:2939 | (a) approval under this Chapter is sought by written resolution, and
-- src:2940 | (b) a memorandum is required under this Chapter to be sent or submitted to every eligible member before the resolution is passed,
-- src:2941 | any accidental failure to send or submit the memorandum to one or more members shall be disregarded for the purpose of determining whether the requirement has been met.
@ref s 224(1) accidental failure to send the memorandum (src:2938-2941)
GIVEN `approval under this Chapter is sought by written resolution` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a memorandum is required under this Chapter to be sent or submitted to every eligible member before the resolution is passed` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the failure to send or submit the memorandum to one or more members was accidental` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 224(2) subsection (1) has effect subject to a provision of the articles` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 224(1) the failure is disregarded in determining whether the requirement has been met` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (NOT `approval under this Chapter is sought by written resolution`) OR (NOT `a memorandum is required under this Chapter to be sent or submitted to every eligible member before the resolution is passed`)
        THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where— (a) approval under this Chapter is sought by written resolution, and (b) a memorandum is required under this Chapter to be sent or submitted to every eligible member before the resolution is passed, any accidental failure ... shall be disregarded"
        IF NOT `the failure to send or submit the memorandum to one or more members was accidental`
        THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "any accidental failure to send or submit the memorandum"
        IF `s 224(2) subsection (1) has effect subject to a provision of the articles` EQUALS JUST TRUE
        THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): "subject to any provision of the company's articles" (what the articles provide is not in the text)
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- ======================================================================================================================
-- s 225 Cases where approval is required under more than one provision
-- ======================================================================================================================

-- src:2944 | (1) Approval may be required under more than one provision of this Chapter.
@ref s 225(1) approval may be required under more than one provision (src:2944-2944)
GIVEN `the number of provisions of this Chapter under which approval is required` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 225(1) approval is required under more than one provision of this Chapter` MEANS
    IF `the number of provisions of this Chapter under which approval is required` GREATER THAN 1
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Approval may be required under more than one provision of this Chapter"

-- src:2945 | (2) If so, the requirements of each applicable provision must be met.
@ref s 225(2) the requirements of each applicable provision must be met (src:2945-2945)
GIVEN `s 225(1) approval is required under more than one provision of this Chapter` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the requirements of each applicable provision have been met` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 225(2) approval has been given as this Chapter requires` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `s 225(1) approval is required under more than one provision of this Chapter` EQUALS NOTHING
        THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "If so, the requirements of each applicable provision must be met" (approval is not required under more than one provision)
        IF `the requirements of each applicable provision have been met`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the requirements of each applicable provision must be met"

-- src:2946 | (3) This does not require a separate resolution for the purposes of each provision.
@ref s 225(3) no separate resolution for each provision (src:2946-2946)
GIVEN `s 225(1) approval is required under more than one provision of this Chapter` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 225(3) a separate resolution is required for each provision` MEANS
    IF `s 225(1) approval is required under more than one provision of this Chapter` EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "This does not require a separate resolution for the purposes of each provision"
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "This does not require a separate resolution" speaks of the case where approval is required under more than one provision
